---
title: How to Triage Feedback
sidebar:
  order: 12
---
**The Feedback tab is where new bugs, feature requests, change requests, and client-submitted items wait for a first look. Nothing lands on your board or backlog until someone accepts it — or declines it, or merges it into an existing item.**

### **Where Items Come From**

Anything can end up needing triage, no matter how it was created — internally, by your team, or from a client. Every item in the queue shows an **origin** badge so you know where it came from:

- **Client** — submitted by a client through their portal.
- **Internal** — created by your team.
- **AI** — generated by Taskip's AI task generator.
- **Import** — added through a CSV import.
- **Workflow** — created automatically by a workflow automation.

An item's **type** (Task, Bug, Feature, Feedback, or Change request) is separate from where it came from — a bug report can come from a client or from your own team, for example. The Feedback tab lists anything still waiting for triage, regardless of its type.

### **Opening the Feedback Tab**

Open a project and select **Feedback** from the tab bar. The tab shows a count badge whenever items are waiting, and it updates live as new items arrive — you don't need to refresh the page. Clients never see this tab; they see the status of their own submissions elsewhere.

### **Reading the Queue**

Each row shows:

- A **type icon** and the item's **title** (with its task key, if it has one).
- An **origin** badge.
- A **similar** badge (for example "2 similar") when Taskip's duplicate check finds items that look alike.
- The **priority** flag, the requester's avatar, and how long it's been waiting (for example "3d").

Filter the queue by **Type**, **Origin**, or **Age** (1 day, 3 days, 7 days, 30 days, or all), and sort it by Oldest, Newest, or Priority. Select multiple rows with their checkboxes to accept or decline them together.

### **Accepting an Item**

Accepting turns a pending item into planned work in one step. Click the checkmark on a row (or press **a** with it focused) to open the accept form, where you can set:

- **Type** — change it if it was miscategorized.
- **Priority**
- **Stage** — which board column it lands in (defaults to your first To do stage).
- **Estimate** — an optional time estimate.
- **Assignees**

Click **Confirm** to accept it. Nothing here is required — leave a field as-is and Taskip uses the item's current type, its existing priority, and your project's first To do stage.

### **Declining an Item**

Click the **X** on a row (or press **d**) to decline it. Choose a reason — **Won't do**, **Duplicate**, **Cannot reproduce**, or **Invalid** — and optionally add a message the requester will see explaining why. Declined items leave the queue and move into your Done column with a "Declined" chip, so they don't stay in your active columns.

### **Merging Duplicates**

If an item looks like a repeat of existing work, click the merge icon (or press **m**) to open the merge picker. Taskip suggests likely duplicates first, ranked by match percentage; you can also search by title or task key. Confirm a target and the source item is closed as a duplicate, linked to the item you merged it into. Its comments, files, labels, and watchers move over to the target automatically — nothing is lost, and anyone who was watching the original is added to the item that replaces it.

### **Keyboard Shortcuts**

The Feedback tab is fully usable from the keyboard:

| Key | Action |
| --- | --- |
| `j` / `k` | Move focus down / up the list |
| `a` | Accept the focused item |
| `d` | Decline the focused item |
| `m` | Merge the focused item |
| `o` or `Enter` | Open the focused item |
| `Esc` | Close whatever's open |

### **After Triage**

Once accepted, declined, reopened, or merged, the same controls follow the item onto its task detail page — a banner above the title shows its triage status (for example "Awaiting triage" with Accept/Decline buttons, or "Declined" with a Reopen button) so you don't need to come back to this tab to act on it later. Anyone who submitted an item can withdraw it themselves while it's still pending.

### **Who Can Triage**

Any staff member can open the Feedback tab and see what's waiting. Accepting, declining, and merging are limited to Admins, Managers, and Project Managers (or a project Lead) — a Member without that access will see a permission error if they try.

